{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1795628885,"nonce":"zPNqHwCcjuIYmFc2i8gwcoXiZHw=","title":"A rebuild that only moves or resizes children leaves them with their old classes","message":"`update_subtree_layout_from_builder` (renderer/build/subtree.rs), the patch for a `RebuildKind::LayoutProps` stateful rebuild, replaces each child's layout style, render props and handlers but never registers the new element's classes. The visual-only path does. A node reused for a different element keeps the first element's class, and the stylesheet passes that follow style it as that.\n\nReproducer: a focused code editor, press and then drag along a line. The current-line box is patched into the selection box. It keeps `blinc-code-active-line`, so the selection is painted with `--primary` at 5% instead of `--selection`, and `.blinc-code-selection` finds nothing.\n\nTest: `blinc_recorder/tests/code_editor_selection_drag.rs` asserts the box's background after a drag.","files":null}]}